<h1>Panel</h1>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">The slide-out panel is only rendered when the <code>:l_ui_panel_body</code> content block is present. Click the panel button in the bottom-right corner to see it in action, or use <kbd>⌘i</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+i</kbd> to toggle it.</p>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">Draggable button</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">The panel toggle button can be repositioned by dragging it with a mouse or touch. You can also double-click it to cycle through corners. The position is saved to <code>localStorage</code> and restored across sessions.</p>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">You can also snap the button to corners with keyboard shortcuts: <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + 1</kbd> (top-left), <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + 2</kbd> (top-right), <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + 3</kbd> (bottom-left), <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + 4</kbd> (bottom-right).</p>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">A short tap (under 5px of movement) toggles the panel as normal. The panel itself can always be toggled with <kbd>⌘i</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+i</kbd>.</p>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">For full control, override the partial by creating <code>app/views/layouts/layered_ui/_panel.html.erb</code> in your application.</p>

<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-lg"><code>&lt;% content_for :l_ui_panel_heading do %&gt;
  &lt;h2&gt;Side Bar&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;

&lt;% content_for :l_ui_panel_body do %&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;This is the panel body content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
